1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:05,631
You would never fix your car with the mechanic on the phone, but that is how you code with an AI chatbot.

2
00:00:05,931 --> 00:00:07,737
A coding-agent session fixes that.

3
00:00:08,237 --> 00:00:10,602
A chat assistant is the mechanic on the phone.

4
00:00:10,902 --> 00:00:11,996
He can only talk.

5
00:00:12,296 --> 00:00:16,505
So you paste his fix into your code, run it, and carry the error back to him.

6
00:00:16,805 --> 00:00:17,700
Again and again.

7
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:22,418
A coding agent is the mechanic standing in your garage, with tools.

8
00:00:22,718 --> 00:00:25,484
You give it one job, in your terminal or your editor.

9
00:00:25,784 --> 00:00:26,869
Then it works in a loop.

10
00:00:27,169 --> 00:00:28,306
It reads your files.

11
00:00:28,606 --> 00:00:29,580
It edits the code.

12
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,728
It runs a command, and checks the result.

13
00:00:32,028 --> 00:00:32,892
Still broken?

14
00:00:33,192 --> 00:00:35,667
It goes around again, until the job is done.

15
00:00:35,967 --> 00:00:39,337
That whole visit, every step and every result, is one session.

16
00:00:39,837 --> 00:00:41,260
You stop being the messenger.

17
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,638
You watch, and you can stop it at any moment.

18
00:00:44,588 --> 00:00:47,016
It can still be wrong, so give it a test to run.

19
00:00:47,316 --> 00:00:48,553
But notice what changed.

20
00:00:48,853 --> 00:00:50,733
The mechanic did not get a bigger brain.

21
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:53,405
He got hands, and a way to check his own work.

22
00:00:53,705 --> 00:00:55,270
That is what makes it an agent.

23
00:00:55,770 --> 00:00:57,171
Subscribe for the next one.
